# Aeris Terminal

Aeris Terminal is a local-first desktop trading terminal built with Rust and GPUI. It brings charts, order books, market data, and multi-pane workspaces into one native application process.

## Development

The desktop is currently in development mode. Sign-in and automatic updates are disabled while the account and release backends are unconfigured. Provider data still requires valid provider credentials.

Requirements: the Rust toolchain in `rust-toolchain.toml` and the platform dependencies for GPUI. On Linux, run `tools/setup_linux_desktop.sh`.

```text
cargo run --release -p aeris_desktop -- --workspace-tabs
```

## Project layout

- `apps/desktop`: native application
- `crates/market_runtime` and `crates/account_runtime`: in-process runtime owners
- `crates/ui`: design system and chart integration
- `crates/adapters`: market-data providers
- `tools`: development and verification utilities

Nucleus Charts is a pinned Git dependency and is fetched by Cargo.

## Checks

```text
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings
```

See `AGENTS.md` for contributor and architecture rules. This project is proprietary.
